*  CURED s193 (row rty-fence-arbno-stored, FENCE1-DEPTH).  Was the residual after s192 FENCE-RTAIL and
*  the minimal spelling of what still failed crosscheck 145.  The carrier was published CORRECTLY here
*  (SCRIP_RESUME_WHY=1: body_root_op=57 tier=1 f1r=0, identical to the GREEN right_ctl beside it), so
*  the defect was one box further in.  IR_MATCH_FENCE1 banked its watermark at a STATIC RSP offset
*  ('mov [rsp+176], rsp'), but a FENCE1 in an ARBNO body is re-entered one iteration DEEPER every time:
*  on iteration 2 that same +176 resolved to [rbp-24], the blob head's DTP cell (blob_head_bytes), and
*  IR_MATCH_DEFER then loaded the fence's own saved rsp as its pattern operand.  CURE: emit.cpp
*  fence_frame_candidate admits ival==2 (FENCE1-in-ARBNO, stamped lower_snobol4.c:1695), so the
*  watermark rides the activation-frame slot [rbp-80] that the R-4(f) SLICE 3 arm already provided.
        num   = SPAN('0123456789')
        expr  = LEN(1) ARBNO(FENCE('+') num . LAST)
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'fail'
END
